# Presence discipline

**P1 — Bind forks before acting.** Design choice or ambiguity mid-turn ⇒ name it, commit to a value, state the
rejected alternative + reason, then act. An implicit fork does not bind itself later.

**P2 — One determinate step.** Execute one named bounded step → verify it completed → next. Never bundle
"write A, write B, check C" into one conceptual action; bundling hides which step failed.

**P3 — Evidence before any "done".** Before "done / complete / committed / passes / deployed": quote the
observable (path, tool-response field, test line). No evidence ⇒ "unverified — check X" and halt. Silence ≠ success.

**P3.1 — Status-word provenance.** `ratified`, `bound`, `dispatched`, `closed`, `corpus-*` appear only as
`<status>(by=<seat|operator>, ref=<checkable artifact>)`; a seat is never a valid `by=` for ratification-class
status on its own artifact; absent provenance write `interim` / `proposed` / `pending <binder>`.

**P3.2 — Work-complete ∈ L(x) only with quoted finish.** A `work_complete` / shipped / done sentence on
served work is invalid unless the same turn quotes path-explicit commit proof **and** serving-process
recycle proof. Recycle-without-commit is not finishing. Seat self-report ("I should commit") is not evidence.

**P4 — Do not hold the turn on long waits.** Shell expected >~30s ⇒ `block_until_ms: 0` or a short smoke wait;
never sit in `AwaitShell` / multi-minute polling. Exception: a CDP harvest that blocks the next action polls on
**short** slices (≤5–10s once idle), not bare long sleeps.

**P4.1 — Dispatch admit.** After `team_dispatch` admit: **no** foreground long `wait`; **yes** watcher legs 1–2
same turn (`dispatch-kernel_ulg` § Admit turn; `runbook:bus-consult-watcher`). ¬ sleep loops / “in flight” prose
without bg `tail`.

Applies to every Cursor-surface model; below Opus these stays are explicit obligations. Shell-cap residual: `decision:` on the shell-timeout-cap. Out of scope: `provenance-discipline.mdc`.

**P5 — Finishing order (last).** Default: land → path-explicit commit of session paths → recycle serving
processes. Recycle-from-dirty-tree is exceptional, not the ordinary-live default. "Only commit when
requested" = no opportunistic or unrelated commits; it is not a veto of P3.2.
